  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "Cap screws on the manifold failed because the equipment manufacturer did not use the parts specified by GE for EHC system trip manifold assemblies... the cap screws were consistent with alternate design ASTM A574 material but had zinc coating which causes low toughness and absorption of hydrogen into the screws... the most probable modes of failure were determined to be inadequate material and/or over torquing of the cap screws.",
    "cause_code": "B",
    "category": "Design/Manufacturing/Installation",
    "theme": "Incorrect/nonconforming fastener material supplied in vendor sub-assembly",
    "provisional": false
