  "notes": "No inoperable SSCs contributed to the event; EFW actuation was an expected response to low SG level following the turbine/reactor trip, not itself a failure. Turbine system (TA) and steam inlet valves (FCV) to HP/LP turbine are mentioned only in the Safety Significance passage describing EHC/turbine design interface (what would happen if pressure decreased further) -- treated as design context per rule 6, but FCV was still modeled as a Component since it is explicitly EIIS-tagged and part of the safety-significance discussion of this specific failure path; no BACKED_UP_BY edges asserted since no operable backup system is stated for this design-basis trip path. No previous similar event was identified (explicitly stated), so no stub LER/SIMILAR_TO edge emitted."
